    {
      "id": "2063837417464045910",
      "title": "I agree with all of your points. I think vision alone can serve as an effective proxy and may be sufficient to achieve a 95% success rate, but force/torque (F/T",
      "body": "I agree with all of your points. I think vision alone can serve as an effective proxy and may be sufficient to achieve a 95% success rate, but force/torque (F/T) sensing is likely necessary to reach 99.99% reliability.\n\nI know it ultimately depends on the application though. For example, for a home robot, natural language understanding and instruction following may be more important metrics than task success rates alone. However, my personal view is that Physical AI robots will first see widespread adoption in environments where robots have already been used for years, such as manufacturing. In those settings, a 99.99% success rate is typically considered non-negotiable.",
      "url": "https://x.com/s1wase/status/2063837417464045910",
      "author": "2605288466",
      "published_at": "2026-06-08T04:15:59",
      "observed_at": "2026-09-10T03:54:55.605607",
